#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Retraction-consistency gate. See RESULTS.md section 65 and ledger #284-#286.
#
# NOT INSTALLED BY DEFAULT. This file is committed so it is visible and reviewable;
# installing it is a separate, deliberate act:
#
#     ln -sf ../../hooks/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit
#
# Fires only when a document that can carry a retracted claim is staged. Checks that
# every pattern in RETRACTIONS.tsv appears with a retraction marker within six lines,
# so a retraction made once stays visible wherever the retracted figure is stated.
#
# Bypass a single commit with:  git commit --no-verify   (and say why in the message)
set -u
REPO="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 0
cd "$REPO" || exit 0
WATCHED='^(RESULTS\.md|LEDGER\.md|README\.md|RETRACTIONS\.tsv|papers/.*\.md)$'
git diff --cached --name-only | grep -qE "$WATCHED" || exit 0
PY=".venv/bin/python"
[ -x "$PY" ] || PY="$(command -v python3 || true)"
[ -n "$PY" ] || { echo "pre-commit: no python found; skipping retraction check" >&2; exit 0; }
if ! "$PY" -I src/check_retractions.py; then
  cat >&2 <<'MSG'

pre-commit: BLOCKED by the retraction-consistency check.

A retracted claim is stated somewhere without a retraction marker within six lines.
Either annotate it where a reader meets it, or - if the claim is no longer retracted -
remove its row from RETRACTIONS.tsv and record that in the ledger.

This is the failure the project repeated three times (#262, #283, section 65).
Override with: git commit --no-verify
MSG
  exit 1
fi
